From 9d6fe7b4bc294093a65fd735e23f6249ff7cb667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:17:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/21] Capture bounded Manifest-scoped code items without
 exact selectors

Accept Framework-selected executable candidates while retaining method safety checks, no-execute interception, configured budgets, and code-item attribution from the actual method.

Constraint: Force capture must never execute the target method body and must reject runtime, proxy, abstract, native, or code-less methods.

Rejected: Reapply the single exact selector inside ART | It would discard the bounded Manifest namespace candidates selected by Framework.

Confidence: high

Scope-risk: moderate

Directive: Keep force-candidate validation and capture metadata derived from the reflected ArtMethod.

Tested: r0dump F7 class-loader-walk and F8 force-invoke source tests; diff checks.

Not-tested: Full ART native unit-test suite was not rerun for this commit.
Change-Id: I75aa794635f8fb077aaa7f4e5deff930f665b927
